    "basis": "PLAN 3.5 asks for the COARSEST level whose uncertainty is acceptable for a surrogate-training dataset, not certification. Between gci_C and gci_M the outputs move cdp 25.63 %, cd 14.14 %, cmy 1.55 %, cdv 1.42 %, cl 0.58 %. The coarsest level is proposed because the campaign arithmetic is what shapes this decision -- PLAN 0.9: 100 designs is about 8 days of solving -- and because these movements are what the dataset must CARRY as a stated uncertainty, not what it must eliminate.",
